"##########################
"### Vim Editor Options ###
"##########################

" Set file encoding
set encoding=utf-8

" Show line numbers
set number

" Show relative line numbers
set relativenumber

" Turn on syntax highlighting
syntax on

" Turn on bottom ruler (line number; column number)
set ruler

" Allows mouse clicks to change the cursor position
set mouse=a



"############################
"### Text Editing Options ###
"############################

" Enable spell check highlighting
" set spell



"######################
"### Search Options ###
"######################

" Use case-sensitive search, only when a capital letter is used, otherwise case-insensitive
set smartcase

" Show match as search proceeds
set incsearch

" Enable search highlighting
set hlsearch



"#######################
"### Tab Key Options ###
"#######################

" Maximum character width of an actual tab character (measured in spaces)
" You might want to make this significantly different from shiftwidth to differentiate tabs from spaces if expandtab is disabled
set tabstop=4

" The size of an "indent" created, measured in spaces
set shiftwidth=4

" A non-zero value will make the Tab key insert a combination of tabs and spaces to match the tabstop width
set softtabstop=0

" Insert spaces characters instead of tab characters when Tab key is pressed
set expandtab

" Move cursor to the indented beginning of the line (i.e. only preceded by whitespace)
set smarttab

" New lines will automatically have the same indentation as the previous line
set autoindent

" Indents react to the syntax of code you are editing (autoindent should also be enabled if this is on)
set smartindent


"########################
"### "Shortcut Hacks" ###
"#######################
" Enables `:w!!` as "I forgot sudo when editing and now i can't save" to elevate privlages & save.
cmap w!! %!sudo tee > /dev/null

